From: Jon Pretty <jon.pretty@propensive.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 13:59:32 +0200
Subject: Infer the capture set of recursive-implicit dictionary instances

A memoized recursive/by-name implicit is emitted as a synthetic dictionary
class with `val $_inst = new <dictionary>`. Under capture checking, if a
memoized entry is capability-typed, `new <dictionary>` captures those
capabilities, but the val was typed with the bare dictionary class type and so
rejected the capturing constructor with `Found: <dict>^{...} Required: <dict>`.

Type the instance val's tree as inferred (`inferred = true`) so capture
checking solves its capture set from the constructor rather than forcing the
pure class type. Pure dictionaries infer an empty set and are unchanged; only
the capability-carrying case, which previously did not type-check, is affected.

Written with LLM assistance (Claude Code); reviewed content.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Proscala-Patch: dictcaps
